            "review_text": "Justnitid\nMumbai, India368 contributions\n0\nAuthentic local cuisine at an unpretentious family run restaurant\nDec 2019 • Couples\nWe stumbled upon this place by chance on our second evening in Ha Noi while wandering along the narrow streets of the Old Quarter looking for a decent place to dine.\nThere was a look of authenticity about this place - the various meats and dishes on display, the womenfolk bustling about and the few patrons enjoying their dinner. We walked in.\nAlthough it was almost closing time, we were served cheerfully and only a very polite request to order any extras before they closed the kitchen and make the payment upfront.\nThe food was excellent - we ordered a Bun Bo, stir fried veggies and a chicken fried rice.\nHighly recommended to anyone visiting Ha Noi!\nRead more\nWritten February 16, 2020",
