            "review_text": "Thikshan A\nNew York City, New York106 contributions\n1\nThe best food in Vietnam\nDec 2019 • Friends\nThe food was so good we ate here several times. If you are from Singapore, Malaysia or Sri Lanka and similar places you will like the food here. Let me also add it compares well to restaurants in NY, London and Paris. A restaurant the late Anthony Bourdain would be proud of, simply for its flavor. If your a foody- a must. \nThe patrons are a healthy mix of locals and internationals (mainly European). Highly recommend the following combinations\n- seafood soup\n- Grilled Ribpork with five tastes \n- Egg fried rice\n- spicy prawn (Tôm Rang Sót Cay)\n- morning glory (fried Kan Kung - Rau Muóng Xào)\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 8, 2019",
